# 1.3) Run the Pipeline and Check Results

On this page, you'll run the pipeline and verify the pipeline graph, data quality results, and the final Gold table.

## Task 1 - Run the pipeline

1. Click **Run pipeline** at the top of the screen.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-01-run-pipeline.png', 'Run pipeline') }}

2. Progress appears in the bottom panel. It takes a few minutes for serverless compute to start and all 7 tables to be created. Wait until the status changes to **Completed**.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-02-run-completed.png', 'Run completed') }}

!!! tip "Dry run"
    Select **Dry run** from the dropdown next to **Run pipeline** to validate code syntax and table dependencies without processing actual data.

## Task 2 - Check the pipeline graph

1. Click the **Pipeline graph** tab in the bottom panel. Verify the dependencies of the 7 tables flowing from Bronze → Silver → Gold.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-03-pipeline-graph.png', 'Pipeline graph') }}

2. Click the `{{ s.gold.table }}` node in the graph to preview sample data.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-04-graph-preview.png', s.gold.table ~ ' preview') }}

## Task 3 - Check results and data quality by table

1. Click the **Tables** tab in the bottom panel. Verify the row counts processed by each table.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-05-tables-tab.png', 'Tables tab') }}

2. Verify that the Silver table results match below. Some rows were removed per Expectations.

    | Table | Bronze rows | Silver rows | Removed |
    |---|---|---|---|
{% for src in s.sources %}
    | {{ src.name }} | {{ src.rows | num }} | {{ src.silver.rows | num }} | {{ (src.rows - src.silver.rows) | num }} |
{% endfor %}

3. Click `{{ s.sources[0].silver.table }}` to see violations per Expectation.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-06-01-expectations.png', 'Expectations results 1') }}

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-06-02-expectations.png', 'Expectations results 2') }}
{% if s.pipeline.expectations_note %}

    !!! info "{{ s.pipeline.expectations_note.title }}"
        {{ s.pipeline.expectations_note.body | indent(8) }}
{% endif %}

## Task 4 - View the Gold table in Catalog Explorer

1. Click **Catalog** in the left sidebar, then expand `{{ cat }}` → `default`. Verify that all 7 tables created by the pipeline are present.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-07-catalog-tables.png', '7 tables in Catalog Explorer') }}

    !!! tip "Find your catalog quickly"
        If there are many catalogs, type `{{ cat }}` in the search box above the tree. Only your catalog stays in the list.

2. Click `{{ s.gold.table }}` and verify in the **Overview** tab that column comments and primary key (`{{ s.gold.primary_key }}`) are registered.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-08-gold-overview.png', s.gold.table ~ ' Overview') }}

3. Click the **Sample Data** tab to view data summarized as {{ s.gold.grain }}. Total row count is {{ s.gold.rows | num }}{{ s.gold.rows_note }}.

    {{ shot('01-lakeflow-pipeline/1-3-09-gold-sample-data.png', s.gold.table ~ ' Sample Data') }}

!!! success "Congratulations!"
    You've completed {{ de.name | poss }} work. You've cleansed source data to create Silver and Gold tables the analytics team can trust. In the next Step, you'll become {{ da.title | role }} {{ da.name }} and {{ ('build a dashboard using `' ~ s.gold.table ~ '`') if s.options.dashboard else 'define business metrics as Metric Views' }}.
